  "reason": "Evidence: The two best experiments (config_008: 0.725, config_019: 0.721) both use scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer aggregation, with only a marginal difference between weighted and concat fusion. The RNA encoder (scvi_n200 >> scgpt) and aggregation (transformer) are well-supported, but the image encoder has only been tested as imagenet_vit_l. Question: Does swapping the image encoder to resnet50 (a CNN vs ViT architecture) maintain or improve performance? config_013 is a clean single-variable change from the best config (config_008), isolating the image encoder effect. Why this is the best use: With 5 experiments remaining, confirming or ruling out the image encoder as a performance lever is critical—if resnet50 matches or beats ViT-L, we gain flexibility for later fine-tuning; if it underperforms, we lock in imagenet_vit_l and can focus remaining budget on subtler hyperparameters (aggregation, fusion, profile setting)."
